# Copy to sharing.env (git-ignored) to build a release with Sharing on your own
# backend (see SELF_HOSTING.md). tool/build_apk.sh, build_bundle.sh,
# build_deb.sh and build_linux_release.sh pass it with --dart-define-from-file
# when the file exists, and the Android build reads NTV_SHARE_HOST from it for
# the App Link host. If any value is empty, the build has no Sharing.
#
# NTV_SHARE_URL: your Supabase project's address,
#   https://<project ref>.supabase.co (Project Settings -> Data API -> Project URL).
NTV_SHARE_URL=
# NTV_SHARE_KEY: the project's publishable key, sb_publishable_... (Project
#   Settings -> API Keys), or the legacy anon key. It is public by design;
#   row-level security protects the data. Never put the secret key here.
NTV_SHARE_KEY=
# NTV_SHARE_HOST: the host that serves invite_page/, with no scheme or path,
#   e.g. invites.example.org or <user>.github.io. Invite links are
#   https://<host>/ntv/i/<CODE>.
NTV_SHARE_HOST=
